          "questions": [
            {
              "number": 12,
              "localNumber": 12,
              "stem": "What methods do some advertisements trumpet about changing a habit?",
              "options": {
                "A": "Those involving no self-recognition.",
                "B": "Those forcing us to clench our teeth.",
                "C": "Those resisting various temptations.",
                "D": "Those requiring no willpower at all."
              },
              "answer": "D"
            },
            {
              "number": 13,
              "localNumber": 13,
              "stem": "What does the speaker define willpower as?",
              "options": {
                "A": "Regulating one's actions for the sake of good health.",
                "B": "Controlling one's actions with a motivating thought.",
                "C": "Using practical examples to guide one's behavior.",
                "D": "Denying oneself any comfort to prevent diseases."
              },
              "answer": "B"
            },
            {
              "number": 14,
              "localNumber": 14,
              "stem": "What may sound amazing enough as regards willpower?",
              "options": {
                "A": "It equips us with an expert skill.",
                "B": "It exerts an enduring force on us.",
                "C": "It leads to a burning goal.",
                "D": "It begins with a bright idea."
              },
              "answer": "D"
            },
            {
              "number": 15,
              "localNumber": 15,
              "stem": "What does the speaker say may make for effective willpower?",
              "options": {
                "A": "Any cherished goal.",
                "B": "Any positive mindset.",
                "C": "Any personal instinct.",
                "D": "Any valued role model."
              },
              "answer": "A"
            }
          ],
          "transcript": [
            "You may have seen advertisements trumpeting methods of changing a habit that require absolutely no willpower whatsoever.",
            "But can you really change a bad habit or create a good one without willpower?",
            "To answer this question we first have to ask, what is willpower?",
            "Most people sadly think of it only as the ability to clench their teeth and resist attractive temptations.",
            "In this view, willpower means self-denial and no fun.",
            "No wonder people hope to make changes without it.",
            "I define willpower as using only the thought of your motivators to control your actions.",
            "Let's say your motivators are prevent diabetes and reach a healthy weight.",
            "So if you are at the all-you-can-eat buffet, you think about your motivator, avoid diabetes through weight loss, and you take small portions and avoid the dessert table.",
            "So amazingly enough, willpower begins with a thought, a bright idea, some way to improve your life or contribute to others.",
            "This bright idea is your motivator.",
            "Dr. Walter Mischel, an expert on willpower skills, uses the expressive term, a burning goal.",
            "Whether you call it a motivator, a burning goal, or a bright idea, this idea is the force behind your willpower.",
            "What sort of bright ideas motivators make for effective willpower?",
            "In fact, any goal that you value strongly counts.",
            "The list may include good health, self-respect, a better future for your family, personal mission, and being a role model for your child.",
            "All these can certainly drive a positive change."
          ],
