          "transcript": [
            "Conversation two",
            "M: Today I'm talking to the renowned botanist Jane Forster.",
            "F: Thank you for inviting me to join you on the show, Henry.",
            "M: Recently, Jane, you've become quite a celebrity since the release of your latest documentary.",
            "M: Can you tell us a little about it?",
            "F: Well, it follows my expedition to study the vegetation indigenous to the rainforest in equatorial areas of Southeast Asia.",
            "M: You certainly get to travel to some very exotic locations.",
            "F: It was far from glamorous, to be honest.",
            "F: The area we visited was accessible only by canoe, and the living conditions in the hut were primitive, to say the least.",
            "F: There was no electricity, and our water supply was a nearby stream.",
            "M: How were the weather conditions while you were there?",
            "F: The weather was not conducive to our work at all, since the humidity was almost unbearable.",
            "F: At midday, we stayed in the hut and did nothing.",
            "F: It was too humid to either work or sleep.",
            "M: How long did your team spend in the jungle?",
            "F: Originally, we planned to be there for a month, but in the end, we stayed for only two weeks.",
            "M: Why did you cut the expedition short?",
            "F: Halfway through the trip, we received news that a hurricane was approaching, and we had to evacuate at very short notice.",
            "M: That sounds like a fascinating anecdote.",
            "F: It was frightening.",
            "F: The fastest evacuation route was through river rapids.",
            "F: We had to navigate them carrying all of our equipment.",
            "M: So overall, was the journey unsuccessful?",
            "F: Absolutely not.",
            "F: We gathered a massive amount of data about the local plant life.",
            "M: Why do you put up with such adverse conditions?",
            "F: Botany is an obsession for me.",
            "F: Many of the destinations I visit have stunning scenery, and I get to meet a variety of people from all over the world.",
            "M: So where will your next destination be?",
            "F: I haven't decided yet.",
            "M: Then we can leave it for another occasion.",
            "F: Thanks.",
            "What do we learn about the man from the conversation?"
          ],
