          "transcript": [
            "Conversation 1.",
            "F: Wow, I would give anything to be more like Audrey Hepburn.",
            "M: I never really understood why so many girls were such big fans of her.",
            "M: I mean, I've seen the famous films, Roman Holiday, Breakfast at Tiffany's, and a few others, but I still don't fully get it.",
            "M: Was she that great of an actress?",
            "F: Well, for me, my adoration goes beyond her movies.",
            "F: She had such a classic elegance about her.",
            "F: She was always so poised, in part because she spent years training as a ballet dancer before becoming an actress.",
            "M: Why didn't she stick to dancing as a career?",
            "F: It seems it was fate.",
            "F: She suffered from inadequate nutrition during the war, and therefore a career as a professional dancer would have been too demanding on her body.",
            "F: So she focused on acting instead.",
            "F: Roman Holiday was her first big break which made her a star.",
            "M: Was that the film that opened with her shopping for jewelry in New York City?",
            "M: You know, the scene she was wearing a black dress and dark sunglasses with a pearl necklace and long black gloves?",
            "M: I see the photo of her in that costume everywhere.",
            "F: No, that one is Breakfast at Tiffany's.",
            "F: That costume is often referred to as the most famous little black dress of all time.",
            "F: Her character in that film is very outgoing and charming, even though in real life, Audrey always described herself as shy and quiet.",
            "M: So what did she do after her acting career?",
            "F: She dedicated much of her life to helping children in need.",
            "F: Her family received international aid during the war when she was growing up.",
            "F: I think that left a big impression on her.",
            "F: That's where I got the idea to volunteer for children's charity next weekend.",
            "M: I'll join you.",
            "M: I may not be as charming as Audrey Hepburn, but I'm all for supporting a good cause."
          ],
